1
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:11,160
Khun Irene doesn't know we have
a backup shutdown key for A382.

2
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:13,000
Good thing you had us make one.

3
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:14,480
Ai!

4
00:00:17,480 --> 00:00:18,840
Let that robot go.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,440
In exchange, I’ll create
a new daughter for you.

6
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:23,440
What have you done to Ai?!
Why is she like this?!

7
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:24,600
Go ask Irene.

8
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:31,240
Don’t worry.

9
00:00:32,479 --> 00:00:33,640
I’ll take care of you.

10
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:38,960
if I’m gone...
please don’t forget me.

11
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:41,160
You have to be happy, okay?

12
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:44,200
How am I supposed to be happy without you, Ai?

13
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:46,320
I’m sorry.

14
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:30,280
This is the best way.

15
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:20,960
Good morning, Ai.

16
00:02:26,079 --> 00:02:28,000
Wake up. It’s already morning.

17
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:34,960
Didn’t you tell me humans should
get up and get their morning vitamin D?

18
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:38,920
So you should wake up and recharge too.

19
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:15,040
Hey, Ai.

20
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:18,840
I think I'll get some pad
kraphao from Auntie Kai's today.

21
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:22,720
Then I'll go pick up some groceries.
We've run out of pretty much everything.

22
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:25,720
Oh, and I need to water the plants too.

23
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:27,560
I don't know how long I've neglected them.

24
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:30,160
The roses have all wilted,

25
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:33,360
even though that was supposed to be your job.

26
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:08,800
So...

27
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:12,840
you still haven't woken up today.

28
00:06:25,400 --> 00:06:27,400
Ugh, P’ Zoon! I can't take it anymore.

29
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:30,480
What? What's wrong, honey?
Need to use the bathroom?

30
00:06:30,520 --> 00:06:33,920
Just go. Our place is just over there.
Want me to come with you?

31
00:06:34,040 --> 00:06:36,320
No, I don't need the bathroom.

32
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:37,960
I'm talking about Gen.

33
00:06:37,960 --> 00:06:40,720
You saw her the other day.
She looked so miserable

34
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:42,960
like the world was gonna be
overrun by zombies tomorrow.

35
00:06:43,440 --> 00:06:44,960
Huh? Zombies are invading tomorrow?

36
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:47,240
Then we need to stock up on food,

37
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:49,920
build a wall, put up
barbed wire, dig a bunker...

38
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:51,280
What game is it this time?

39
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:52,760
What?!

40
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:55,320
What game?
How much did you spend?

41
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:57,480
You're playing with Josh,
aren't you? Confess now!

42
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:58,480
No, no! I didn't top up—

43
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:05,360
Ai Zoon, just come clean.
It'll get Wan off your back.

44
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:07,520
If I admit it, I'm dead!

45
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:08,640
So you did top up!

46
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:11,200
Weren't we talking about Gen, honey?

47
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:13,680
I'll deal with you later.

48
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:18,960
Hey, I don't know anything.

49
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:23,320
Seriously? You don't know?

50
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:26,400
Yeah. I'm staying out of Gen's business.

51
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:32,080
It's fucking hot.

52
00:07:32,880 --> 00:07:34,920
This is why I hate working mornings.

53
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:42,840
Did I miss something?

54
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:46,320
Auntie Kai said she's
staying out of Gen's business.

55
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:50,080
Ohhh…

56
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:55,360
See for yourselves.

57
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:57,480
Hey, P' Gen!

58
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:00,880
P’ Gen!

59
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:02,480
What?

60
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:04,760
What'd you buy all that for?

61
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:07,240
Household stuff.

62
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:09,240
Have you eaten?

63
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:12,240
No. I forgot.

64
00:08:12,840 --> 00:08:16,680
How about some pad kaphrao, your favorite?
Auntie wants to sell you some.

65
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:20,240
Maybe another day.
I'm not hungry yet.

66
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:23,520
Where’s P’ Ai?

67
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:41,440
See?

68
00:08:41,799 --> 00:08:45,120
I told you, P’ Gen answers
anything you ask now.

69
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:47,880
No complaining, no yelling, no nothing.

70
00:08:48,480 --> 00:08:49,480
Except for one thing.

71
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:52,840
If you bring up that girl,

72
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:55,880
Gen looks like her whole world’s falling apart.

73
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:57,560
She won’t answer a thing.

74
00:08:58,920 --> 00:09:00,400
So I just leave her alone now.

75
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:03,640
Didn’t she cry when you asked her the other day?

76
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:06,360
That’s why you’ve been holding your tongue.

77
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:08,360
Yeah. I didn't know.

78
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:12,880
I'm not asking her anymore.
You guys shouldn't ask her either.

79
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:18,240
Since she's like this,
it only means one thing.

80
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:21,760
- She got dumped.
- For sure.

81
00:12:16,640 --> 00:12:18,080
I promised you...

82
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:21,640
I'd take care of you myself.

83
00:12:25,160 --> 00:12:26,080
It's okay.

84
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:31,520
I can still keep going.

85
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:19,440
I'm here, P’ Ploy.

86
00:13:19,920 --> 00:13:21,720
Yeah, just wait there.

87
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:24,600
Mm. Just call me when you get here.

88
00:13:25,520 --> 00:13:27,880
Wait, Gen. Are you okay?

89
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:32,680
I'm okay.

90
00:13:34,360 --> 00:13:35,800
I'm back to work, just like before.

91
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:38,320
Still trying to prove myself to Mom.

92
00:13:40,680 --> 00:13:42,000
A girl's gotta eat, right?

93
00:13:43,120 --> 00:13:44,840
So send plenty of work my way.

94
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:47,760
You know that's not what I meant.

95
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:50,520
Have you come to terms with what happened to Ai?

96
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:55,120
You know I never could.

97
00:13:56,760 --> 00:13:59,400
But I've never been the type
to give up easily. You know that.

98
00:14:00,400 --> 00:14:02,920
I know. I know that very well.

99
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:05,400
So calm down, okay?

100
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:07,840
I don’t need to calm down.

101
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:10,760
I'm already calmer than a monk.

102
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:13,400
Then just talk to her nicely, okay?

103
00:14:15,640 --> 00:14:16,640
She said…

104
00:14:18,720 --> 00:14:19,800
she wanted to talk to you.

105
00:14:27,560 --> 00:14:28,640
What are you doing here?

106
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,120
Shall we talk?

107
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:52,040
Are you angry with me?

108
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:53,080
Why did you do it?

109
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:59,160
I thought you'd have calmed down by now.

110
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:01,880
But I guess not.

111
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:03,160
I asked why you did it!

112
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:06,240
Why did you kill Ai?
What did you do that for?!

113
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:11,320
You hurt someone you created
with your own hands, when she...

114
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:13,880
when she called you her mom!

115
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:16,600
How could you kill your own child?

116
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:18,520
Well? Answer me!

117
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:25,560
Don't you think this was the best way out?

118
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:32,720
Watching someone you love die
right in front of you is the best way out?

119
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:36,920
Have you ever truly loved anyone?

120
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:39,280
How can you say something so messed up?

121
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:45,480
Ai is a robot.

122
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:49,480
You'll be the one to die first anyway.

123
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:52,560
No matter how much I help this robot,

124
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:54,160
the two of you will have
to part ways eventually.

125
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:55,240
I love Ai.

126
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:01,480
And I don't care what she is.

127
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:03,840
Because I love her.

128
00:16:14,360 --> 00:16:15,800
Wouldn’t it be better if it were me?

129
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:21,840
Y-you…

130
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:23,560
We look identical.

131
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:26,320
So why can’t it be me?

132
00:16:33,440 --> 00:16:39,000
Are you sure you drew Ai because
you saw her in your dreams?

133
00:16:41,160 --> 00:16:44,080
Why didn’t you consider
that we might have met before?

134
00:16:48,160 --> 00:16:51,160
PAY: Ms. Irene Thanakarn
***20 MILLION BAHT***

135
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:54,320
The minister is unable to meet with you.

136
00:16:57,640 --> 00:16:59,920
This is the support you've
been owed over the years.

137
00:17:02,080 --> 00:17:05,839
From now on, he'll transfer money
into your account every month.

138
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:10,680
In exchange for what?

139
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:16,640
He doesn't want you…
interfering with his new family.

140
00:17:22,160 --> 00:17:25,200
If there's nothing else,
I'll take my leave.

141
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:56,480
Oh, sorry!

142
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:00,280
Excuse me.

143
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:04,440
Did you forget something?

144
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,080
Is there something wrong?

145
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:19,720
Oh, nothing. I just think
you're really beautiful.

146
00:18:30,520 --> 00:18:31,480
What happened?

147
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:37,280
Oh, nothing. I just think
the girl earlier was really beautiful.

148
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:39,800
And I only caught a glimpse of her.

149
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:46,360
Oho, what’s going on?

150
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:48,440
What? Nothing.

151
00:18:48,600 --> 00:18:50,400
- Was she pretty?
- Don't be silly!

152
00:18:50,440 --> 00:18:52,040
- Really?
- Come on, it’s nothing!

153
00:18:57,080 --> 00:18:59,560
Back then, I felt like I never
should've come back to Thailand.

154
00:19:00,480 --> 00:19:02,200
I shouldn't have looked for my real father.

155
00:19:04,800 --> 00:19:07,920
And just as I was thinking
what to do with that check…

156
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,480
you handed it back to me.

157
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:19,440
And it made me realize...
why let it go to waste?

158
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:25,280
The price of my heartbreak that day
could be used for so much.

159
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:32,960
You might not remember me...

160
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:39,120
but I recognized you
the moment I saw your profile.

161
00:19:43,400 --> 00:19:46,280
Where did you see it? From P' Ploy?

162
00:19:50,200 --> 00:19:51,640
You might not know

163
00:19:51,640 --> 00:19:54,400
that Khun Ploy has to send us
everyone's profiles for review first.

164
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:57,600
It's strange.

165
00:19:58,760 --> 00:20:02,040
Anyone can generate
images with AI these days...

166
00:20:04,520 --> 00:20:06,320
but your work is far more special than that.

167
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:11,480
You sketch it first,
then process it in the program.

168
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:16,320
That's why I always look
forward to seeing your work.

169
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:22,440
Besides, we can be sure no face like
this exists anywhere else in the world.

170
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:28,240
I thought I just liked your work...

171
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:34,960
until I saw your latest piece.

172
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:39,680
I...

173
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:43,080
drew you.

174
00:20:45,960 --> 00:20:47,000
Yes.

175
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:54,400
It's one of the few times in my life
I felt glad I came back to Thailand.

176
00:21:43,640 --> 00:21:44,640
Can't it be me?

177
00:21:48,600 --> 00:21:50,160
Will you let me love you in her place?

178
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:08,720
What exactly are you going to do?

179
00:22:18,040 --> 00:22:19,200
Will Ai really be safe?

180
00:22:20,080 --> 00:22:22,920
Safe or not, I'm the only
one you can depend on.

181
00:22:22,960 --> 00:22:23,800
Irene!

182
00:22:26,840 --> 00:22:28,000
You have to trust me.

183
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:30,240
I'm the only one who can save her.

184
00:22:31,200 --> 00:22:33,960
Like you're the only one who can
shut her down and erase her memories?

185
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:38,200
My command wasn't to shut Ai down.

186
00:22:41,320 --> 00:22:42,440
What do you mean?

187
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:47,280
If anyone forces her to
shut down without this ring,

188
00:22:47,880 --> 00:22:49,520
she'll do a fake shutdown.

189
00:22:55,080 --> 00:22:57,840
And no matter how smart
they are, they'll never notice.

190
00:22:59,320 --> 00:23:03,240
And if anyone tries to reset her
system or tamper with her memories,

191
00:23:03,800 --> 00:23:07,600
I've backed up all of Ai's
memories up to that day in here.

192
00:23:09,760 --> 00:23:12,160
So that means you can wake Ai back up, right?

193
00:23:46,280 --> 00:23:50,040
Hey! Stop it!
Can't you see she's in pain?!

194
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:05,920
Ai! Hey! Let me go!

195
00:24:08,800 --> 00:24:10,880
Ai!

196
00:25:00,120 --> 00:25:02,880
Ai, wake up.

197
00:25:03,640 --> 00:25:04,760
Wake up already.

198
00:25:06,640 --> 00:25:07,920
Come on, wake up.

199
00:25:17,320 --> 00:25:18,280
Wake up, Ai.

200
00:25:19,440 --> 00:25:20,400
Wake up already.

201
00:25:21,600 --> 00:25:23,160
You've been sleeping for way too long.

202
00:25:30,520 --> 00:25:31,400
Please wake up.

203
00:25:37,680 --> 00:25:38,600
Gen…

204
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:52,720
Please don’t cry.

205
00:25:54,240 --> 00:25:55,920
Did I do something wrong again?

206
00:25:59,720 --> 00:26:01,240
There, there.

207
00:26:03,920 --> 00:26:06,760
When did I ever teach you to say that?

208
00:26:07,560 --> 00:26:11,600
I learned it on my own
because I don't want you to cry.

209
00:26:15,320 --> 00:26:17,000
There, there.

210
00:26:19,400 --> 00:26:24,600
~ Until the day I met you ~

211
00:26:25,200 --> 00:26:29,240
~ You came and broke down my walls ~

212
00:26:29,240 --> 00:26:32,800
~ Now I know that good love looks just like you ~
Thank you, Ai.

213
00:26:32,840 --> 00:26:35,720
~ I’m glad that we found each other ~
Thank you for coming back.

214
00:26:35,720 --> 00:26:39,920
~ Your love feels like a dream ~
I’m back.

215
00:26:39,960 --> 00:26:43,240
~ Whatever tomorrow may bring ~

216
00:26:43,280 --> 00:26:45,480
~ Whether it’s good or bad ~

217
00:26:45,480 --> 00:26:49,960
~ I believe everything will be alright ~

218
00:26:49,960 --> 00:26:53,480
~ Because I have you who understands me ~

219
00:26:58,960 --> 00:27:00,080
Is this really okay?

220
00:27:02,720 --> 00:27:04,320
Will you let me love you in her place?

221
00:27:07,840 --> 00:27:08,560
No.

222
00:27:12,640 --> 00:27:13,560
Why?

223
00:27:15,440 --> 00:27:18,160
We look identical,
and I'm a real person.

224
00:27:18,760 --> 00:27:19,960
I can be with you.

225
00:27:20,360 --> 00:27:21,400
Because you’re not Ai.

226
00:27:24,480 --> 00:27:27,320
The one I love is Ai,
not someone named Irene.

227
00:27:29,280 --> 00:27:30,920
Even if you're identical twins,

228
00:27:32,760 --> 00:27:35,640
the one I love is Ai, not you.

229
00:27:44,560 --> 00:27:45,680
It's better this way.

230
00:27:55,200 --> 00:27:58,760
This is why I fell in love with her.

231
00:28:25,240 --> 00:28:26,880
Finally home.

232
00:28:27,640 --> 00:28:30,160
I thought those tests would never end.

233
00:28:36,680 --> 00:28:38,360
Why are you standing there?

234
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:43,400
How much… do you remember?

235
00:28:49,680 --> 00:28:50,680
Everything.

236
00:29:19,320 --> 00:29:21,040
Actually, I heard everything.

237
00:29:23,400 --> 00:29:24,400
What did you hear?

238
00:29:31,240 --> 00:29:34,800
The day you shut me down,
I was aware of it.

239
00:29:44,240 --> 00:29:48,520
But at that time, I just felt like
something was put into my brain,

240
00:29:49,680 --> 00:29:52,040
and some program was deleted.

241
00:29:53,360 --> 00:29:56,960
It was the tracking program.

242
00:30:02,480 --> 00:30:06,160
But what was added was a dataset that Mother...

243
00:30:12,960 --> 00:30:14,720
that Khun Irene sent over.

244
00:30:16,760 --> 00:30:20,920
And it only started working
after I was shut down by Father.

245
00:30:27,240 --> 00:30:28,320
I  wasn’t dead.

246
00:30:29,520 --> 00:30:32,680
So... you still haven't woken up today.

247
00:30:36,360 --> 00:30:37,560
I wasn’t broken.

248
00:30:39,280 --> 00:30:41,520
This is Ai, the one I love.

249
00:30:45,880 --> 00:30:47,640
I just entered hibernation mode.

250
00:30:57,720 --> 00:30:59,200
I may have been asleep…

251
00:31:00,280 --> 00:31:00,880
Ai.

252
00:31:02,680 --> 00:31:04,120
I miss you so much.

253
00:31:04,520 --> 00:31:05,800
...but I heard everything.

254
00:31:07,720 --> 00:31:08,760
I can still keep going.

255
00:31:17,320 --> 00:31:18,720
Everything.

256
00:31:33,960 --> 00:31:35,280
I heard everything.

257
00:31:37,400 --> 00:31:38,880
I wanted to wake up...

258
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:42,800
and open my eyes for you.

259
00:31:45,080 --> 00:31:46,280
But I couldn't do it.

260
00:31:51,600 --> 00:31:52,800
I’m sorry.

261
00:31:54,840 --> 00:31:57,600
I'm sorry I made you suffer so much, Gen.

262
00:31:58,160 --> 00:31:59,400
I wasn't suffering.

263
00:32:02,120 --> 00:32:03,120
You were tired.

264
00:32:03,440 --> 00:32:04,640
I was willing to be.

265
00:32:08,120 --> 00:32:10,000
But I made you cry.

266
00:32:12,680 --> 00:32:14,560
Aren’t you crying too?

267
00:32:35,680 --> 00:32:37,320
From now on, let's cry together.

268
00:32:38,200 --> 00:32:39,840
We'll be sad together?

269
00:32:40,600 --> 00:32:41,600
And laugh.

270
00:32:44,720 --> 00:32:46,240
Be happy together.

271
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:48,160
And fight with each other.

272
00:32:50,800 --> 00:32:52,040
No.

273
00:32:53,280 --> 00:32:55,520
I don't want to fight with you.

274
00:32:56,000 --> 00:32:57,040
That's impossible.

275
00:32:58,080 --> 00:32:59,720
If we live together,
we're bound to fight.

276
00:33:02,200 --> 00:33:03,440
Why is that?

277
00:33:08,760 --> 00:33:10,720
Because from now on,
we'll cry together,

278
00:33:12,040 --> 00:33:13,280
be happy together,

279
00:33:14,320 --> 00:33:16,840
fight, and then make up.

280
00:33:18,360 --> 00:33:21,480
Living life like this... how's that sound?

281
00:33:33,120 --> 00:33:34,200
Why is it that,

282
00:33:35,960 --> 00:33:40,680
even when you say we'll be crying together...

283
00:33:43,440 --> 00:33:45,440
I feel so happy?

284
00:34:02,840 --> 00:34:04,240
Because I love you.

285
00:34:28,840 --> 00:34:30,480
The whole time I was asleep,

286
00:34:31,800 --> 00:34:33,600
I wanted to tell you this...

287
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:37,360
this feeling...

288
00:34:41,280 --> 00:34:43,120
I love you too.

289
00:35:12,200 --> 00:35:14,320
- What are you guys doing?
- Shh! Keep it down!

290
00:35:16,200 --> 00:35:17,360
You're gonna break my neck!

291
00:35:17,360 --> 00:35:19,160
You're lucky Zoon didn't break your neck.

292
00:35:19,400 --> 00:35:21,560
Otherwise, I'll wring your neck myself, Ai Josh.

293
00:35:22,040 --> 00:35:24,800
Keep it down!
Gen's gonna hear us.

294
00:35:25,240 --> 00:35:27,600
I thought you guys were done
prying into P’ Gen's business.

295
00:35:28,160 --> 00:35:29,920
I said keep it down!

296
00:35:29,960 --> 00:35:32,440
Yeah, we were about to stop.

297
00:35:32,680 --> 00:35:34,120
But who would've thought…

298
00:35:34,160 --> 00:35:36,240
The pretty girl would come back.

299
00:35:48,320 --> 00:35:49,680
Ai Gen! We're all soaked!

300
00:35:50,120 --> 00:35:51,120
Damn right you are.

301
00:35:51,600 --> 00:35:54,880
Why, you! Is that any
way to talk to your elders?

302
00:35:55,120 --> 00:35:57,800
And what are you elders doing here, may I ask?

303
00:35:58,080 --> 00:36:01,520
I was just watering my plants in my own house.
Why'd you stick your heads in, then?

304
00:36:01,600 --> 00:36:02,720
To pry, obviously.

305
00:36:03,760 --> 00:36:04,680
Okay.

306
00:36:05,760 --> 00:36:06,840
- P’ Zoon!
- Josh!

307
00:36:07,320 --> 00:36:11,200
Prying hours are over.
Kindly return to your homes.

308
00:36:12,120 --> 00:36:13,760
What are you here to pry into today?

309
00:36:13,760 --> 00:36:17,080
Oh, Nong Ai! Hearing you
say “pry” breaks my heart.

310
00:36:17,280 --> 00:36:18,920
Ai Gen! What have you been teaching her?

311
00:36:20,360 --> 00:36:21,640
Gen didn't teach me.

312
00:36:21,920 --> 00:36:24,200
You pick things up when you
spend a lot of time together.

313
00:36:25,240 --> 00:36:27,880
We're a couple.
It's only natural we'd be alike.

314
00:36:33,840 --> 00:36:35,320
Why did you tell them that?

315
00:36:36,120 --> 00:36:37,720
The whole village will know by tomorrow.

316
00:36:38,320 --> 00:36:41,840
Good, then I won't have to go
around announcing that I'm back.

317
00:36:42,640 --> 00:36:44,080
I'll leave that to you guys.

318
00:36:44,920 --> 00:36:46,240
Come on, let’s get inside.

319
00:36:50,200 --> 00:36:51,320
The kid's got guts.

320
00:36:51,680 --> 00:36:53,120
Yeah. Gotta hand it to her.

321
00:36:53,840 --> 00:36:55,120
Whose house should we hit first?

322
00:36:55,520 --> 00:36:58,200
How about the garden this evening?
Everyone will be there.

323
00:36:58,800 --> 00:36:59,480
Let’s go.

324
00:37:00,320 --> 00:37:03,720
Alright, guys. The whole
village needs to hear about this.

325
00:37:03,760 --> 00:37:05,320
- Alright, Auntie!
- Get to it, Josh!

326
00:37:05,320 --> 00:37:06,000
Let’s go!

327
00:37:42,400 --> 00:37:43,400
You've gotten bolder.

328
00:37:44,720 --> 00:37:45,720
Is that a bad thing?

329
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:49,600
I'm not punishing you.
I'm rewarding you.

330
00:38:08,080 --> 00:38:09,560
If you're going to reward me...

331
00:38:11,880 --> 00:38:13,440
you'll have to give me more than that.

332
00:38:15,480 --> 00:38:16,480
How much more?

333
00:38:48,080 --> 00:38:49,640
You like taking my clothes off for me.

334
00:38:52,880 --> 00:38:54,760
So I'll let you do it.

335
00:38:57,680 --> 00:38:59,400
Since when did you become such a tease?

336
00:39:03,320 --> 00:39:04,640
Because I had a teacher.

337
00:39:05,760 --> 00:39:07,520
And who might that teacher be?

338
00:39:08,600 --> 00:39:09,720
Good question.

339
00:39:13,400 --> 00:39:15,440
I was hoping my teacher
would continue the lesson.

340
00:42:04,360 --> 00:42:06,640
You know I don't have to eat, Gen.

341
00:42:13,760 --> 00:42:16,800
Who said I was making any for you?
I'm eating this all by myself.

342
00:42:20,160 --> 00:42:21,240
You'll get fat.

343
00:42:22,040 --> 00:42:23,960
Didn't you complain about gaining weight?

344
00:42:25,560 --> 00:42:27,280
But you said you didn't want to eat.

345
00:42:28,840 --> 00:42:31,920
Who said that?
I just said I don't have to eat.

346
00:42:32,600 --> 00:42:35,880
That's why I said you didn't have to eat.

347
00:42:41,240 --> 00:42:43,200
Mmmm.

348
00:42:45,080 --> 00:42:47,440
Still as chewy and tender as ever.

349
00:42:49,280 --> 00:42:51,800
Should I share some with you?

350
00:42:51,800 --> 00:42:54,160
Or maybe, I'll just eat it all myself.

351
00:42:56,440 --> 00:42:57,360
Smells good.

352
00:43:04,920 --> 00:43:06,480
Didn't you say you didn't have to eat?

353
00:43:07,680 --> 00:43:09,000
I was worried you'd get fat.

354
00:43:18,000 --> 00:43:19,160
You’re way too cute.

355
00:43:27,040 --> 00:43:28,080
What's with the smile?

356
00:43:32,120 --> 00:43:34,440
What? Trying to beg for some noodles?

357
00:43:34,560 --> 00:43:36,280
Not a chance.
I'm eating them all myself.

358
00:43:38,120 --> 00:43:40,560
Can I have some too?

359
00:43:40,600 --> 00:43:43,040
What? I made enough for one.
It's all mine.

360
00:43:43,080 --> 00:43:46,640
There's no way you can
eat all that. Let me help you.

361
00:43:46,680 --> 00:43:47,680
Be cute and ask.

362
00:43:50,880 --> 00:43:52,480
Please…

363
00:43:53,920 --> 00:43:55,240
Pretty please.

364
00:43:55,560 --> 00:43:56,400
Pretty please.

365
00:43:56,960 --> 00:43:59,440
Please, let me have some too.

366
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:00,800
More.

367
00:44:03,960 --> 00:44:05,480
Come on, that’s enough!

368
00:44:11,760 --> 00:44:15,080
Of course. We can do
everything we discussed last week.

369
00:44:16,440 --> 00:44:17,240
Okay.

370
00:44:20,440 --> 00:44:21,160
Yes.

371
00:44:24,760 --> 00:44:26,480
Alright, I'll let you know.

372
00:44:28,320 --> 00:44:30,000
Let me call you back.

373
00:44:32,480 --> 00:44:34,080
Hey. Ai?

374
00:44:34,560 --> 00:44:36,360
You're back, beautiful!!

375
00:44:39,000 --> 00:44:41,640
How are you?
When did you wake up?

376
00:44:42,120 --> 00:44:43,560
Why didn't you tell me?

377
00:44:44,040 --> 00:44:45,240
Do you know how worried I was?

378
00:44:46,160 --> 00:44:47,520
Weren’t you worried about me too?

379
00:44:49,000 --> 00:44:50,520
I was worried about both of you.

380
00:44:51,240 --> 00:44:54,200
You went completely silent.
I was about to lose my mind.

381
00:44:55,280 --> 00:44:56,800
I was worried about both of you too.

382
00:44:57,360 --> 00:44:59,040
C’mere, let me give you a hug.

383
00:45:04,040 --> 00:45:05,240
Someone's possessive.

384
00:45:05,320 --> 00:45:06,520
Mm. I’m possessive.

385
00:45:09,600 --> 00:45:11,880
I'm sorry I didn't let Gen call and tell you.

386
00:45:12,800 --> 00:45:14,080
I wanted to come here myself.

387
00:45:14,240 --> 00:45:17,160
It's okay. I'm just glad you're awake.

388
00:45:17,800 --> 00:45:21,640
Do you know what Gen was like
while you were asleep?

389
00:45:25,560 --> 00:45:29,480
Oh Ai, didn't you have something
to ask P’ Ploy? Go ahead.

390
00:45:32,320 --> 00:45:34,480
Do you need someone to
analyze data for you, P’ Ploy?

391
00:45:35,840 --> 00:45:37,560
Well, I do.

392
00:45:38,640 --> 00:45:39,640
Why do you ask?

393
00:45:41,840 --> 00:45:46,840
Don't you think the perfect person for
the job is standing right in front of you?

394
00:45:50,120 --> 00:45:51,440
I'd like to ask you for a job.

395
00:45:52,040 --> 00:45:54,480
I want to take care of Gen
the way she took care of me.

396
00:45:54,720 --> 00:45:58,480
Do you have a position for
a robot who's only a few months old

397
00:45:58,520 --> 00:46:00,560
but exceptionally good at analyzing data?

398
00:46:01,720 --> 00:46:02,600
You’re hired.

399
00:46:03,040 --> 00:46:03,800
Sis.

400
00:46:04,360 --> 00:46:05,200
Hire her now.

401
00:46:08,600 --> 00:46:09,560
My company.

402
00:46:10,320 --> 00:46:11,520
So you're not gonna hire her?

403
00:46:12,560 --> 00:46:14,200
Didn't you say you were drowning in work?

404
00:46:16,400 --> 00:46:17,680
Hmmm…

405
00:46:19,280 --> 00:46:20,600
Hmmm…

406
00:46:25,640 --> 00:46:27,000
Of course I'm hiring you!

407
00:46:27,440 --> 00:46:28,760
Seriously.

408
00:46:28,800 --> 00:46:31,880
With skills like that,
you'd be perfect for the job.

409
00:46:32,800 --> 00:46:35,720
But... we'll negotiate the salary later.

410
00:46:38,920 --> 00:46:41,920
How about you start next week?

411
00:46:48,880 --> 00:46:52,720
Listen. If P’ Petch ever gets
handsy with you again, punch him.

412
00:46:53,320 --> 00:46:54,440
P’ Ploy won’t mind.

413
00:46:57,200 --> 00:46:58,880
That's the tenth time you've said that.

414
00:46:59,000 --> 00:47:00,240
Because I’m mad!

415
00:47:03,720 --> 00:47:07,200
I think P’ Petch was just
trying to mess with you.

416
00:47:09,080 --> 00:47:10,320
That’s why I’m mad!

417
00:47:20,560 --> 00:47:21,880
Are you tired?

418
00:47:23,000 --> 00:47:24,760
We can always meet my friend another day.

419
00:47:26,240 --> 00:47:27,600
We talked about this.

420
00:47:28,920 --> 00:47:30,960
I want to be a part of your life.

421
00:47:32,040 --> 00:47:34,680
Besides, you said this friend important to you.

422
00:47:35,640 --> 00:47:38,120
I want to get to know the
important people in your life too.

423
00:47:50,240 --> 00:47:53,200
Oh, there they are.
Perfect timing.

424
00:48:15,760 --> 00:48:18,160
Come on. I'll introduce you to them.

425
00:48:24,080 --> 00:48:26,480
This is P' Le and Rann.
Rann's my best friend.

426
00:48:26,960 --> 00:48:30,480
And this... is Ai. The person I love.

427
00:48:31,640 --> 00:48:32,720
We know.

428
00:48:39,720 --> 00:48:40,760
How cute.

429
00:48:45,640 --> 00:48:47,200
Where are you taking me, Gen?

430
00:48:47,960 --> 00:48:49,680
It's scary being blindfolded like this.

431
00:48:49,920 --> 00:48:50,920
Come on.

432
00:48:56,160 --> 00:48:57,040
Ready?

433
00:48:58,200 --> 00:48:59,200
No.

434
00:48:59,480 --> 00:49:00,160
Huh?

435
00:49:01,120 --> 00:49:03,160
Just kidding. I’m ready.

436
00:49:04,280 --> 00:49:05,600
You’re unbelievable.

437
00:49:09,080 --> 00:49:09,760
Alright.

438
00:49:11,000 --> 00:49:11,840
One…

439
00:49:13,800 --> 00:49:14,680
Two…

440
00:49:14,920 --> 00:49:15,680
Three!

441
00:49:30,880 --> 00:49:34,680
Finally... my work is
being exhibited in a gallery.

442
00:49:42,800 --> 00:49:43,720
Don’t like it?

443
00:49:45,520 --> 00:49:48,520
This woman is my inspiration.

444
00:49:54,520 --> 00:49:55,760
You mean...

445
00:49:56,480 --> 00:49:57,480
It’s you.

446
00:50:01,560 --> 00:50:03,280
I painted this based on you.

447
00:50:04,440 --> 00:50:09,360
~ Until the day I met you ~

448
00:50:10,240 --> 00:50:14,160
~ You came and broke down my walls ~

449
00:50:14,160 --> 00:50:16,680
I've been searching for the woman
from my dreams my whole life,

450
00:50:18,040 --> 00:50:19,520
and now I’ve finally found you.

451
00:50:38,520 --> 00:50:39,320
Gen.

452
00:50:42,480 --> 00:50:44,000
Are you satisfied now?

453
00:50:46,400 --> 00:50:47,400
What do you think?

454
00:50:49,840 --> 00:50:53,920
Your heart rate and external
reactions indicate that

455
00:50:54,240 --> 00:50:55,760
you're not lying.

456
00:50:58,360 --> 00:51:00,520
You still haven't stopped scanning me?

457
00:51:02,120 --> 00:51:03,160
Just kidding.

458
00:51:04,440 --> 00:51:08,560
I didn't analyze your heart rate,
scan you, or use any systems.

459
00:51:09,560 --> 00:51:11,000
I only said that because...

460
00:51:12,440 --> 00:51:15,960
I could feel that you really felt that way.

461
00:51:18,800 --> 00:51:20,680
Including...

462
00:51:23,160 --> 00:51:23,960
What?

463
00:51:27,560 --> 00:51:29,360
The fact that you love me more than anything.

464
00:51:38,960 --> 00:51:40,440
Then remember this well:

465
00:51:42,440 --> 00:51:43,760
I love you more than anything.

466
00:51:44,680 --> 00:51:48,240
~ Now I know that good love looks just like you ~

467
00:51:48,240 --> 00:51:51,120
~ I’m glad that we found each other ~

468
00:51:51,160 --> 00:51:55,080
~ Your love feels like a dream ~

469
00:51:55,480 --> 00:51:58,720
~ Whatever tomorrow may bring ~

470
00:51:58,720 --> 00:52:01,040
~ Whether it’s good or bad ~

471
00:52:01,080 --> 00:52:05,480
~ As long as I have you, it will be alright ~

472
00:52:05,520 --> 00:52:08,800
~ Because I have you who understands me ~

473
00:52:18,200 --> 00:52:19,720
Someone once said that

474
00:52:20,920 --> 00:52:23,240
the only thing that waits for no one is time.

475
00:52:24,680 --> 00:52:27,080
But I don't regret any of the time gone by.

476
00:52:28,360 --> 00:52:30,360
After all, my life was far from ordinary.

477
00:52:31,720 --> 00:52:33,800
I've experienced so many things.

478
00:52:35,120 --> 00:52:38,960
I even met a goofy robot who
brightened up my life every single day.

479
00:52:41,240 --> 00:52:42,760
A robot who became a person.

480
00:52:44,880 --> 00:52:46,160
The most important person.

481
00:52:48,560 --> 00:52:49,600
That person...

482
00:52:52,720 --> 00:52:58,560
Thank you for taking care of me for 45 years.

483
00:53:02,320 --> 00:53:04,120
Not this again.

484
00:53:04,480 --> 00:53:05,720
You said it wrong.

485
00:53:07,040 --> 00:53:09,760
We've taken care of each other for 45 years.

486
00:53:11,640 --> 00:53:12,520
Ai…

487
00:53:14,560 --> 00:53:15,360
Yes?

488
00:53:16,600 --> 00:53:17,880
Thank you…

489
00:53:20,440 --> 00:53:23,200
for staying by my side all this time.

490
00:53:29,800 --> 00:53:31,440
You're saying this again.

491
00:53:33,480 --> 00:53:36,840
I... love you.

492
00:53:48,400 --> 00:53:49,440
I know.

493
00:53:51,760 --> 00:53:54,000
You've made me feel it all along.

494
00:53:58,040 --> 00:54:00,000
I’m so tired today.

495
00:54:02,160 --> 00:54:04,160
Let me rest for a bit.

496
00:54:16,480 --> 00:54:17,680
Get some rest.

497
00:54:19,960 --> 00:54:21,440
You've had a long day.

498
00:55:21,880 --> 00:55:23,200
I love you.

499
00:56:08,360 --> 00:56:11,360
English Subtitles by Saowalak K.
